# Trim saved text fields

When saving a text field, store `value.trim()` so leading and trailing whitespace is not persisted.

Trim at save time. Leave the in-progress keystrokes alone so the user can type a space between words.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
name: event.target.value

// ✅ GOOD
name: trimSavedText(event.target.value)
```

Use `trimSavedText()` from `front-ends/front-end-cursor/src/utils/trimSavedText.ts`.

Create-event (`AdminAddEventPage` and its `AddEvent*` sections) already does this. Other pages still need the same treatment.
